*> SELECT * in embedded SQL: in a cursor declared in working-storage,
*> in a statement, after DISTINCT, and in INSERT ... SELECT. COUNT(*)
*> and named columns are fine.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. SELECTS.
DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
    EXEC SQL INCLUDE SQLCA END-EXEC.
    EXEC SQL DECLARE ALL-EMP CURSOR FOR
        SELECT * FROM EMPLOYEE
    END-EXEC.
01  EMP-COUNT          PIC S9(9) COMP.
01  EMP-NAME           PIC X(30).
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
    EXEC SQL SELECT DISTINCT * INTO :EMP-NAME FROM EMPLOYEE
        WHERE ID = 1
    END-EXEC
    IF SQLCODE NOT = 0
        DISPLAY "NO EMPLOYEE"
    END-IF
    EXEC SQL INSERT INTO EMP-ARCHIVE SELECT * FROM EMPLOYEE END-EXEC
    IF SQLCODE NOT = 0
        DISPLAY "NOT ARCHIVED"
    END-IF
    EXEC SQL SELECT COUNT(*) INTO :EMP-COUNT FROM EMPLOYEE END-EXEC
    IF SQLCODE NOT = 0
        DISPLAY "NO COUNT"
    END-IF
    EXEC SQL SELECT NAME INTO :EMP-NAME FROM EMPLOYEE WHERE ID = 2
    END-EXEC
    IF SQLCODE NOT = 0
        DISPLAY "NO NAME"
    END-IF
    DISPLAY EMP-NAME EMP-COUNT
    GOBACK.
